{"id": "https://wineindustryadvisor.com/?p=169278", "url": "https://wineindustryadvisor.com/2026/09/29/realm-cellars-from-struggling-brand-to-top-napa-estate-winery/", "title": "🎧Realm Cellars: From Struggling Brand to Top Napa Estate Winery", "summary": "<img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"432\" src=\"https://win-advisor-media-library.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/29102131/handharvesting-640x432.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 1px;\" title=\"globalwinebank.com\" width=\"640\" /><p><img alt=\"\" class=\"attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image\" height=\"1080\" src=\"https://win-advisor-media-library.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/29102131/handharvesting-scaled.jpg\" title=\"globalwinebank.com\" width=\"1600\" /></p>In the final story of this two-part series, Scott and host Carol Collison talk about Scott’s acquisition of the virtual brand Realm Cellars in 2012. In this interview Scott tells the story of getting into the business, which he partially financed by assuming accumulated debts, and how he then found more debts, less cash, and a daily working capital struggle. After the momentum shift for the brand from a 100-point Parker score, the business finally turned the corner. Today, Realm is an estate winery with properties in the important Napa growing areas of Stags Leap, Pritchard Hill, and Coombsville", "content": "<img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"432\" src=\"https://win-advisor-media-library.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/29102131/handharvesting-640x432.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 1px;\" title=\"globalwinebank.com\" width=\"640\" /><p><img alt=\"\" class=\"attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image\" height=\"1080\" src=\"https://win-advisor-media-library.s3.us-west-1.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/29102131/handharvesting-scaled.jpg\" title=\"globalwinebank.com\" width=\"1600\" /></p>In the final story of this two-part series, Scott and host Carol Collison talk about Scott’s acquisition of the virtual brand Realm Cellars in 2012. In this interview Scott tells the story of getting into the business, which he partially financed by assuming accumulated debts, and how he then found more debts, less cash, and a daily working capital struggle. After the momentum shift for the brand from a 100-point Parker score, the business finally turned the corner. Today, Realm is an estate winery with properties in the important Napa growing areas of Stags Leap, Pritchard Hill, and Coombsville", "published_at": "2026-09-29 22:41:33+00:00", "source_name": "Wine Industry Advisor", "source_type": "media", "language": "en", "content_type": "market_report", "country": "US", "continent": "NEW_WORLD", "region": "Americas/North/USA", "producer_role": "trade_media", "trust_tier": "T3_professional", "info_purpose": ["P2_market_analysis"], "collection_tier": "C1_rss"}
